[ 10 20 30 ] 0 @i .
[ 10 20 30 ] 2 @i .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 0 @i .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 1 @i .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 0 @j .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 2 @j .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 0 0 @i,j .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 1 2 @i,j .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix dup 0 0 @i,j swap 1 2 @i,j + .
3 identity-matrix 0 0 @i,j .
3 identity-matrix 0 1 @i,j . cr
3 int-segment 10.7 0 !i 0 @i .
3 int-segment 7 0 !i 8 1 !i 9 2 !i 2 @i .

cr \ @e / !e: flat row-major element read and store; !i,j: the (row,column) store.
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 0 @e . cr        \ 1
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix 4 @e . cr        \ 5
[ 10 20 30 ] vector 1 @e . cr               \ 20  nx1
[ 10 20 30 ] 1 3 matrix 1 @e . cr           \ 20  1xn, same access
[ 3 1 4 ] vector dup argmin @e . cr         \ 1   argmin's flat index consumed
[ -1 1 ] vector ln 0 @e . cr                \ null: a NaN element reads as null
[ 0 0 0 ] vector 9 1 !e . cr                \ stores in place, leaves the vector
[ 1 2 3 ] vector null 0 !e sort . cr        \ null stores as NaN; sorts last
2 2 0-matrix 7 0 1 !i,j 8 1 0 !i,j . cr     \ (row, column) stores chain

\ === fused stores: compiled words pin the rewritten shapes and their behavior ===
: element-into | target position element | target element position !e drop ;
' element-into see-compiled
[ 0 0 0 ] vector to fused-target
fused-target 1 42 element-into  fused-target . cr    \ 42 at index 1 via (!e.lll0)

: double-into | target position | target  position 2 *  position !e drop ;
' double-into see-compiled
fused-target 2 double-into  fused-target . cr        \ 4 at index 2 via (!e-drop)

: corner-nine | target | target 9 0 1 !i,j drop ;
' corner-nine see-compiled
2 2 0-matrix to fused-block
fused-block corner-nine  fused-block . cr            \ 9 at (0,1) via (!i,j-drop)

\ === fused reads: @e gets every fusion @i has, so a matrix reads as a flat buffer ===
[ 10 20 30 40 ] vector to fused-vector
[ 3 0 2 ] vector to fused-indices
: element-two | m | m 2 @e ;
' element-two see-compiled
fused-vector element-two . cr                        \ 30 via (@e.lit.l0)

: element-swap | m | m swap @e ;
' element-swap see-compiled
3 fused-vector element-swap . cr                     \ 40 via (@e.swap.l0)

: element-over 1 pick swap @e ;
' element-over see-compiled
fused-vector 1 element-over . drop cr                \ 20 via (@e.d)

: element-below 2 pick 2 pick @e ;
' element-below see-compiled
fused-vector 0 99 element-below . drop drop drop cr  \ 10 via (@e.dd)

: gather-at | k | fused-vector fused-indices k @e @e ;
' gather-at see-compiled
0 gather-at . 1 gather-at . 2 gather-at . cr         \ 40 10 30 via (gather.e.l0)

: bump-at | m i | m m i @e f1+ i !e drop ;
' bump-at see-compiled
fused-vector 1 bump-at fused-vector matrix>array . cr    \ [ 10 21 30 40 ] via (inc!i)

: add-at | i d | fused-vector fused-vector i @e d f+ i !e drop ;
' add-at see-compiled
1 2.5 add-at fused-vector matrix>array . cr          \ [ 10 23.5 30 40 ] via (+!i)

\ errors
[ 1 2 3 ] vector 3 @e                       \ (element index out of bounds)
[ 1 2 3 ] vector :x 1 !e                    \ (value must be a float or null)
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix 5 0 2 !i,j           \ (column index out of bounds)
"x" 0 @e                                    \ (not a matrix)
fused-vector 9 bump-at                      \ (element index out of bounds through (inc!i))
2 int-segment 5 100 !i                      \ (segment index out of bounds)
